Forbidden: bare ``idx`` / ``idxs`` as a local, parameter, or attribute name. **Forbidden:** ``indices`` as a naming token (use ``idxs``). **Forbidden bare-result ``_from_``:** ``idx_from_*`` (``idx`` alone is not a result noun) — a label→position table is ``<noun>_idx`` (e.g. ``cell_idx[cell]``); a conversion whose result is a real ``<noun>_idx`` may be ``<noun>_idx_from_<source>`` (e.g. ``cell_idx_from_node_id``). Forbidden: ``node_idx`` / ``node_idxs`` / ``node_idx_from_id`` — the network neuron integer is bare ``node`` / ``nodes``; id→node map is ``node_from_id``. Do not use `id` for an in-memory array position — external keys go through `node_from_id` first. Do not use `index` or `ix`. Do not use bare `i` as an idx abbrev in compounds. Do not use `row` for a cost-entry mask or CSV table row — use `entry` / `entry_mask` or `field`. Do not use `t_idx`, `step_idx`, or `time_idx` — use bare `t`. Do not use `b_idx` — use bare `b`. Do not use `entry_idx` / `entry_idxs` — use bare `entry` / `entries`. Do not use ``slot`` / ``slots`` for any idx or param-axis role.

### `implementation`

Definition: Integration layer that wires the pieces of one large action (session, cost, optimization, persistence, …) into a path that runs through successfully before the top-level ``run`` driver. Module ``train.implementation`` (e.g. ``run_train``).
Example: `fname, outdir, session, result = run_train(...)`
Forbidden: `implement` — use `implementation`. Do not use for the top-level plot/CLI driver (`simulation/run.py`) or for argparse-only parsing (`train.cli`).

### `in`

Definition: Total input to a neuron — light sti (`sti`) plus presynaptic/synaptic contributions. At current level (borst): `i_sti + Σ gE`; at voltage level (hp_lp): `v_in = v_syn + v_sti`. Synaptic input `a_*` param: `a_in`.
